00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:04.040
Abraham: Two of the main areas that
can be vulnerable to attack from

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:07.479
cyber criminals are the hardware
and software of a computer system

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.570
so let’s have a look at these two
areas and how they can be affected.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:15.830
Hardware is the physical components
of a computer system and covers

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:19.979
everything a system needs to function
including computer chips, motherboard,

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:25.420
graphics card, CPU [central processing
unit], ventilation fan, RAM,

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.250
HDD, webcam and power supply etc.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.300
Larger organisations have computer
systems involving large servers such

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.519
as mainframes integrated with storage.

00:00:37.969 --> 00:00:42.379
All electronic devices including
smart appliances, computers and mobile

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:47.379
devices, to large computer systems
are run by semiconductor integrated

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:51.069
circuits, also known as computer
chips and these can be at risk

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:54.780
during the design and manufacturing
process, of being altered maliciously.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.910
Malicious hardware in the form of chips
can remain dormant for months or years

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.990
before being used to launch an attack.

00:01:03.389 --> 00:01:06.730
Often security in 'chip' production
is not always looked upon as an

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:11.029
issue, but this form of hardware
vulnerability can affect devices from

00:01:11.029 --> 00:01:13.449
smart phones to major defence systems.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:17.130
An example of this was the Spectre
and Meltdown vulnerabilities

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.270
that were identified in 2018.

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:24.440
These were design flaws in chips that
have been in production since 1995

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:28.429
that meant criminals could bypass
some of the most fundamental low-level

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:32.649
security mechanisms and access things
like passwords and encryption keys.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:38.320
The Operating system or OS is the
software that enables computer

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.899
hardware to communicate and operate
all the other software that is

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:44.000
subsequently loaded onto the computer.

00:01:45.299 --> 00:01:49.290
Every computer must have at least one
operating system to run other programs.

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:53.340
It speaks the computers language
and therefore talks to the software.

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:57.560
The operating system has many
functions including managing

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:03.010
memory, files, processes, system
and devices and Security of course.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.320
Operating systems should always be
kept up to date to maintain that

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:11.039
security, so regular updates should
be scheduled to protect from malware

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:12.980
threat and unauthorised access.

00:02:14.179 --> 00:02:18.340
As well as keeping the OS updated other
software should be kept up to date so

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:22.350
that any bugs or patches can be added
to keep the software malware free.

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:26.970
There are a range of different operating
systems available, and these will depend

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.100
on the type of computer system being used.

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:33.860
All computers should have a security
system in place with antimalware software.

00:02:34.719 --> 00:02:39.579
This may be part of an internet supplier
package including firewalls and VPN.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:42.790
Or it may be a standalone antimalware
software package which should be

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:45.130
regularly updated or run continuously.

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:49.120
This will seek out any threats
that may affect a computer system.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:53.770
Some users stick to free antimalware
software, but this does not protect a

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:55.609
system as much as paid for programs.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:00.790
Antimalware packages should protect
systems from the latest virus, malware,

00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:06.140
spyware, and ransomware attacks whilst
maintaining a user’s privacy and identity

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:07.710
especially when browsing the web.

